# The synthetic ambient corpus is checksum-verified byte for byte before a single message is
# replayed, so its bytes are content rather than text. Left to the default, a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every newline and the integrity guard fails on a corpus
# nobody edited -- which is the guard working correctly against the wrong question.
demo/fixtures/** -text

# Golden vectors and recorded fixtures are compared byte for byte for the same reason.
tests/**/golden/** -text
